# Path-based routing for the rosters pages, scoped by season slug (see the
# Phase 1 plan's "URL structure" section). These are rewrites (200), not
# redirects -- the URL bar keeps the clean path while Pages serves the
# existing static file. Client-side JS reads location.pathname instead of
# today's ?league=/?team= query params for these routes.
#
# :season/:team matches a single path segment each (no slashes), which is all
# a season slug ("league2627") or team slug ever needs.

# /league2627/matchup/123 -> a specific week's matchup. No matchup.html yet
# (later phase) -- add this once that page exists:
# /:season/matchup/:id   /matchup.html   200

# Rewrite target is "/", not "/index.html" -- Pages' clean-URL canonicalization
# turns a /index.html rewrite target into an outer 308 redirect to "/" instead
# of serving it in place, which defeats the point of a path-based rewrite.
/:season/:team   /   200
/:season         /   200
